From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0048] media: sophgo: unbind SG2002 VPSS from the reserved pool

Partially reverts 0047 for the VPSS driver only; CSI capture and
Coda980 keep their pool binding.

Two reasons:

* rmem_dma_ops has no imported-dmabuf mapping, so a pool-bound device
  rejects every V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF QBUF with ENOMEM. The VPSS node is
  the middle of a zero-copy chain (CSI capture expbuf in, NV12 out to
  buffers the encoder imports), i.e. it is import-only and gets no use
  out of the pool at all. With the default dma_ops both import
  directions work.

* A bare "rmmod sg2002_vpss" wedges the SoC silently on hardware, and
  0047's of_reserved_mem_device_release() — called first, before any
  vb2/v4l2 teardown — is the prime suspect. Not binding the pool takes
  that whole path out of the driver while the run-time stall is being
  chased (see vpss-driver-20260810 campaign notes).

The VPSS block needs no coherent memory of its own: its queues are
driven by imported buffers, and small MMAP-queue test allocations fit
the default CMA.

Signed-off-by: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
index ddffae6..35165fb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
-#include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
@@ -935,11 +934,6 @@ static int vpss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_m2m;
 
-	ret = of_reserved_mem_device_init(&pdev->dev);
-	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
-		dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "failed to initialize reserved memory: %d\n",
-			 ret);
-
 	pm_runtime_enable(&pdev->dev);
 
 	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "registered as /dev/video%d\n", vfd->num);
@@ -956,8 +950,6 @@ static void vpss_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct vpss_dev *vpss = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	of_reserved_mem_device_release(&pdev->dev);
-
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 	video_unregister_device(&vpss->vfd);
 	v4l2_m2m_release(vpss->m2m_dev);
